<page type="text"><layout>Running head at top centre above the text; page number at top left. Two columns of verse in italic, left column long, right column shorter beginning at top right. No marginal notes. A small foot ornament below the left column.; One column of italic verse, right of centre, top to bottom; a black-letter catchword "In" at the lower right below the last line. No margin notes.</layout><page_number>682</page_number><running_head>MYSTERIUM</running_head><bottom_margin><catchword>In</catchword></bottom_margin><main_text><p><i>In opulenta requie,</i><br /><i>De sorte miserorum.</i><br /><i>Vivendo supervacuè:</i><br /><i>Qui charitatem maximè</i><br /><i>Deberent exercere,</i><br /><i>Pra cateris fidelibus</i><br /><i>In omnibus hominibus:</i><br /><i>Virtutes exhibere.</i><br /><i>Cum bonus exemplaribus</i><br /><i>Tam fœminis, quàm mari-</i><br /><i>bus:</i><br /><i>Viam salutis dare:</i><br /><i>Non alta quidem sapere:</i><br /><i>Non fremere, non rapere:</i><br /><i>Non aliquem truffare</i><br /><i>Hæc essent meritoria,</i><br /><i>Servorum Dei gloria,</i><br /><i>Fidelium tutela:</i><br /><i>Per quæ manerêt Principes,</i><br /><i>Et Christiani simplices</i><br /><i>In fidei sequela.</i><br /><i>Sed ubi possunt hæc discerni?</i><br /><i>Cùm nec priores nec moderni</i><br /><i>Pro Deo famulentur:</i><br /><i>Imò pro temporalibus</i><br /><i>Omnes ceu Spiritualibus</i><br /><i>Insistere videntur.</i><br /><i>Majores cum minoribus</i><br /><i>Indocti cum doctoribus</i><br /><i>Et cæteri de clero,</i><br /><i>Non habent rectam speciem,</i><br /><i>Nec curant Cœli pretium,</i></p>
    <p><i>De Christo Deo vero,</i><br /><i>Sub cujus umbra latitant,</i><br /><i>Et sua bona dissipant</i><br /><i>In pompa seculari:</i><br /><i>Sunt PILATI non PRÆ-</i><br /><i>LATI,</i><br /><i>Plus quàm Tyranni depra-</i><br /><i>vati:</i> <i>In virtutibus ignari.</i></p>
  <p><i>Per quos &amp; grex fidelium</i></p>
    <p><i>Tractatur in interitum,</i></p>
    <p><i>Messiâ permittente:</i></p>
    <p><i>Corrupti simul pereunt,</i></p>
    <p><i>Abominabilésque facti sunt</i></p>
    <p><i>Diabolo suadente.</i></p>
    <p><i>Non est qui bonum faciat,</i></p>
    <p><i>Non est qui Deum diligat,</i></p>
    <p><i>Inutiles effecti.</i></p>
    <p><i>Ad munera respiciunt,</i></p>
    <p><i>Justitiam non sitiunt,</i></p>
    <p><i>Delicias illecti.</i></p>
    <p><i>Non vivunt Christianiter,</i></p>
    <p><i>Nec justè, nec humaniter,</i></p>
    <p><i>In seculo præsenti:</i></p>
    <p><i>Ut magna fortalitia,</i></p>
    <p><i>Et plura beneficia</i></p>
    <p><i>Possideant, intenti.</i></p>
    <p><i>Eorum vere spiritus</i></p>
    <p><i>Inanis est, &amp; irritus</i></p>
    <p><i>Ad Dei famulatum:</i></p>
    <p><i>Ab istis omnis gravitas</i></p>
    <p><i>Egreditur, &amp; ruit pravi-tas.</i></p>
  </main_text><notes>The right column is set in shorter lines at top right; the lower part of the page continues beyond this scan. Lower part of the page is cut off; the page ends with the catchword. Some ornamental initials (D, A) read as decorative capitals. The word "pravi-tas" is hyphenated across lines as printed.</notes></page>
